WEBVTT

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:06.810
Crap!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>It's not over.</i>

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.990
<i>If we stop him at first, the game's over.</i>

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.870
All right!

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.420
<i>What the...</i>

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.500
<i>What... did I just do?</i>

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.890
Play!

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.620
<i>No.</i>

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.850
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.350
<i>I'll never get over something like that!</i>

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.400
Strike!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.360
What are you swinging at, Daigo-kun?

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.940
Don't fall apart just because your 
error allowed them to score.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.660
We'll never be able to form a battery

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.850
if you have the mental fortitude 
of a block of tofu, Daigo-kun.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.960
H-Hikaru?

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.060
H-Hikaru?!

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:52.350
Battery Debut!

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.360
Come on, get back in the batter's box.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.940
Oh, uh, sorry.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.060
<i>Why in the world... is Hikaru here?</i>

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.930
Ball!

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.440
That's it.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.290
Good job!

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.440
Keep your eye on the ball.
It's not that fast!

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.460
That guy's so noisy. Who is he?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.520
Oh! It's Hikaru-kun!

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:16.240
Huh?

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.340
What?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.970
Satou's here?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.020
Did you hear that?

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.730
They just said Hikaru-kun was here.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.960
Yeah, looks like it.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:32.140
<i>So you came to cheer him on after all, Hikaru.</i>

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.890
Strike two!

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.940
Mifune Batting 
Center

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.570
Speed

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.570
For both
batting positions

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.570
Right-handed
pitcher

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.070
Home 
run

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.580
Okay.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.090
Looks like you're used to hitting 
100 kmph pitches now.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.460
Let's try this one next.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.210
Speed

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.210
For both
batting positions

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.210
Right-handed 
pitcher

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.210
Wait, why are we moving to slower balls?

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.020
Stop flapping your gums and get in there.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.340
Uh, yes, sir.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:02.970
H-Huh?

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:08.970
It's actually harder to hit a changeup 
than it is to hit a 100 kmph fastball.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.360
For one thing, it arcs, 
so your contact point is smaller.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:17.080
If you get impatient and lean into it, 
your swing won't be as smooth.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:23.580
The changeup is a very basic pitch 
and one you won't hit very far

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.740
unless you've got your batting down.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.670
<i>Gotta be able to swing...</i>

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.870
<i>...at any kind of pitch.</i>

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.430
He did it!

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.930
He's rounded first base!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.060
H-Hey, isn't that a bit risky?!

00:04:58.960 --> 00:04:59.980
Safe!

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.900
That was a close one!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.570
Nice running, Shigeno-kun!

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.440
Nice batting.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.040
Out!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.000
One out, a runner on third.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.140
Daigo-kun's demeanor has changed.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.000
Huh?

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.290
That error was really weighing on 
his mind, but when he saw Hikaru,

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.280
he refocused on the task at hand.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.970
<i>Hikaru came all the way
 here to cheer me on.</i>

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.900
There's nothing wrong with 
a little embarrassment.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.900
But it's definitely wrong to let potential 
embarrassment get in the way of curiosity.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:49.370
Some day, for sure,
we're going to be an invincible battery!

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.240
<i>Hikaru's the one who got
me back into baseball...</i>

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.580
<i>It's time to show him what I can do now!</i>

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.340
Safe!

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.410
All right!

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:07.510
Yes!

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.960
Five runs to four!

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.450
We've taken the lead!

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.980
Mifune

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.980
Tanikawa

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.590
All right, this time, 
we're gonna stay in front!

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.570
Yes!

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.130
Three more outs and the game is ours!

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.810
Yeah!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.460
Hikaru.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.490
Papa.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.280
Were you worried about him?

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:30.660
Yeah.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.420
I was actually planning 
on getting here earlier,

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:38.460
but I showed up late on purpose
to avoid being put on the bench.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:39.810
I see.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.320
Play!

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.470
Strike!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.510
<i>Please, Andy...</i>

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:57.030
<i>Lock it down and end the game here.</i>

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.420
Catcher!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.690
Fair!

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.210
Don't get flustered, Urabe!

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:09.500
You can still make it!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.430
Stop, stop!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:17.740
<i>Phew.</i>

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.640
C'mon, man, what was that all about?

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.650
My mask slipped.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:23.780
What?

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:25.780
When getting the ball, 
you take off the mask!

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:26.950
That's an ironclad rule!

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.840
Y-Yeah, so it is...

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.230
I guess this setup's still new to them.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:36.220
Urabe's not used to 
fielding as a catcher yet.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.500
No outs, a runner on first.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.600
This win won't come easy, that's for sure.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.060
<i>Damn. I won't let him get to second.</i>

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.820
<i>Yes. I can make it!</i>

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:02.370
Andy!

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.200
Time out!

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.960
Unfortunately, it looks like 
you've hurt your calf muscle.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.220
You must've pulled it when you pivoted.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:19.890
It needs icing, and he needs to
go to the hospital right away.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:22.480
Please put in a relief pitcher.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.340
A relief pitcher?

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.060
You say that, but...

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:29.300
I'll take Andy to the hospital.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.920
O-Okay.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:32.040
I'm sorry.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.480
Good luck.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.290
You're heavy.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.470
Sorry.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.660
We've got no choice.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.420
You'll have to pitch, Matsubara.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.290
Y-Yes, sir.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:55.490
This is really bad. He has to pitch with
no outs and runners on first and second?

00:08:58.830 --> 00:08:59.720
Hikaru.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.920
If they let you pitch, would you want to?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:08.070
Play!

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.040
Ball!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.700
<i>This won't work. He's a chicken.</i>

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.550
<i>He hasn't gotten a single strike
since he started warming up.</i>

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:23.610
Ball two.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.830
Ball three.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:38.700
I knew it. Matsubara can't 
handle the pressure.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.590
Tashiro-san.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:43.880
Ball!

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.140
Ball four!

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:46.960
Yes!

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.380
Bases loaded with no outs!

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:52.650
It's over.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.290
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:57.320
<i>We're gonna lose all because of my error.</i>

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:59.070
Time out!

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.410
We're switching pitchers!

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.160
Number 15,

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.070
Satou Hikaru.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.040
<i>H-Hikaru's pitching?</i>

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.560
Wh-What the hell?!

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.920
Hikaru's allowed to play?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:43.440
<i>I asked the manager to name you
on the bench for this game.</i>

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:45.830
<i>It's not breaking any 
tournament rules, either.</i>

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:48.230
<i>Go tear it up out there!</i>

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:50.400
Good job!

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.000
Don't worry.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.710
You can leave everything to me.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.750
B-But you're...

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.510
Hey, what's going on here?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:02.010
You quit the team, so how come 
you're allowed to play?

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.520
Apparently, you can play if you're on the 
team roster before the tournament begins.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.520
I might've moved away, 
but I'm still officially a Dolphins' player.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.100
Wh-What?

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.970
Well, I didn't show up thinking I'd be playing,

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.800
but the team's in a tight spot, 
so I figured, what the hell.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.530
Easy for you to say!

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.890
We're only one run ahead, 
with no outs and bases loaded.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:24.700
If they get one more hit, it's over!

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:27.670
And what's more, you have zero control!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.710
I won't let you just waltz in here 
with your "hero of the hour" spiel,

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.230
only for you to lose the game for us!

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:37.610
Urabe.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.900
I gave him the go-ahead.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:42.570
We don't have any other usable pitchers.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:45.920
All we can do is put our faith 
in Satou and let him pitch.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.740
O-Okay, here you go.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:52.320
To tell you the truth, 
I'm about to throw up.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:53.930
Okay.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.410
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:01.700
<i>My junior baseball career's going to end
with this farce of a game?</i>

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.020
<i>Hikaru.</i>

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.360
Hikaru.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:19.170
If they let you pitch, would you want to?

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.190
N-No.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:25.960
I couldn't just walk on the field 
and butt in on their tournament.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.430
I'm not a part of the team anymore.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.680
It'd make everyone mad.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:32.150
Fine.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:37.700
Then, all you have to do is 
dig them out of this hole.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:41.150
If you help them now,
they'll accept you as a teammate again.

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:46.390
Be honest. You've been itching 
to get up on that mound.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.530
You even have your glove 
in your backpack, didn't you?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:55.300
I learned that you'd been practicing
even after the move back then.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:58.980
When we met up in Gunma 
and I caught one of your pitches,

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:00.990
that's when I knew for sure.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.050
With that kind of pitch, I'm sure you'll 
live up to everyone's expectations!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:14.980
Ouch!

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:21.940
Wow!

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.680
My control's gotten better, 
wouldn't you say, Manager?

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.820
Y-Yeah...

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:32.860
<i>His form and control have improved,
and his pitches are even faster than before.</i>

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.490
You okay, Tobe-kun?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:37.370
Keep your eye on the ball.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.600
Shut up!

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:40.590
And my name's Urabe!

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:48.100
<i>Tch. I was so busy being pissed off, 
I forgot to pay attention to the pitch.</i>

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:58.050
<i>Hikaru.</i>

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.160
<i>That guy...</i>

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.210
<i>Are you freakin' serious?</i>

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:06.730
<i>That ball was so fast, 
I couldn't even see it!</i>

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.000
Come on! You're meant to catch it!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.410
I can't do it!

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:16.680
H-Hey!

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.290
Stop joking around! We don't have 
anyone else who can play catcher!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:23.540
Manager.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:24.710
Huh?

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.970
What is it, Daigo?

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:31.050
Uh, do you want me to play catcher?

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:32.300
What?

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.910
I mean, I want to catch.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.260
Please let me take his place.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:44.240
Those two as a battery...

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:47.070
We're switching catchers.

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.820
Number 13, Shigeno Daigo.

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:52.940
Daigo.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.260
<i>We didn't exchange any words.</i>

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:15.860
<i>I wanted to say something, 
but it was too awkward.</i>

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:23.060
<i>Hikaru probably felt the same way.</i>

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.430
<i>But that was enough.</i>

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:36.980
What's going on?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:40.160
Daigo's catching those monster pitches 
without even batting an eyelid.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.250
Shigeno-kun's been practicing 
his catching for a long time now,

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.440
all so he can catch Hikaru's pitches.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.800
I didn't know that.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:53.800
I didn't think he'd straight up volunteer to 
put himself in the firing line now, though.

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:58.260
This is a pretty intense situation 
for the debut of your battery.

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:00.780
No outs, bases loaded.

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:04.300
If they make just one mistake,
the game is tied.

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:06.150
Play!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.630
<i>I've waited forever for this moment...</i>

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:14.440
See ya, Daigo-kun!

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:16.660
Hey!

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.280
Tomorrow's practice session 
will be our battery debut!

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:27.460
<i>The moment when Daigo-kun 
catches my all-out pitches!</i>

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:34.020
Strike!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.230
Nice throw!

00:16:36.710 --> 00:16:37.850
Time out!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:43.450
You can't use such a big windup
in this situation.

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:44.870
The bases are loaded.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.740
If you're not careful, 
the runner on third will steal home!

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:50.820
Just pitch from the set.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.190
Ah, but...

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.290
What's the "set"?

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:57.780
Like when ramen comes 
with fried rice, you mean?

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.450
You <i>cannot</i> be serious!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.870
Hikaru, he's talking about the set position!

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:07.350
Oh... Oh! The set <i>position!</i>

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:09.880
I know what that is. 
I read about it in a book.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.890
You sure you're gonna be okay?!

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:13.840
Yeah!

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.610
Pitch from the set, right?

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.100
Gotcha.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:18.230
Roger!

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.100
Anyway, I'm counting on you.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.270
Have you ever practiced 
pitching from the set position?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:30.520
If you get it wrong, they'll call a balk
and the runner will score.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.610
It's fine, it's fine!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:35.470
I mean, I don't have a choice, right?

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:37.120
Play!

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.780
<i>Read it in a book, he says...</i>

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.870
<i>Is he going to manage this?</i>

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:46.870
<i>So I think you've got to put your foot 
sideways against the plate.</i>

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:49.670
<i>You then put both hands up in front of you,</i>

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:52.630
<i>and stand still for two or three seconds.</i>

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.030
<i>Yeah, I think that covers it.</i>

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:01.840
Ball!

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.890
Well, it looks like he's 
at least avoided the balk.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:06.810
Yeah.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:12.240
Ball two!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:18.340
But it obviously doesn't come naturally,
and his speed and accuracy have dropped.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:19.660
Oh, no.

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:21.750
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.110
<i>He's not used to pitching from the set.</i>

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.140
<i>But he can't go back to the windup, either.</i>

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.530
<i>It's over.</i>

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.790
Catcher!

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.660
We got lucky with that bounce.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.990
It bounced because 
the juniors use a softer ball.

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.440
But I don't think we can 
rely on that happening again.

00:18:52.640 --> 00:18:54.320
I'm really sorry!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:55.780
Hey!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.490
Satou, your control's as bad
as it always was!

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.100
That's three balls now!

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:01.650
Throw a strike already!

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:08.040
We can't take any more timeouts, either.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.800
At this rate, we'll walk a runner home.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:15.140
We didn't anticipate that he hadn't 
practiced pitching from the set.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:19.800
Hikaru, return to your 
normal style of pitching!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.680
Just do it a bit quicker!

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:24.170
Go back to the windup!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.670
Daigo-kun, are you serious?

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.240
What if they steal home?

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:31.410
No.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.830
Even on a windup,

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:37.400
stealing home would require 
some serious guts.

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:39.680
No outs, bases loaded.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:43.460
The other team won't want to let 
this chance slip away from them.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.660
Given that he couldn't throw
strikes from the set,

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.250
Daigo-kun's probably made the right call.

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.080
Strike!

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:58.820
Yes!

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.360
Three-two.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.380
Full count!

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:05.730
Strike! Out!

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:07.930
He did it! A strikeout!

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:10.930
Okay! One out!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.310
One out, bases loaded.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:16.690
In this situation, they might 
actually go for the steal.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:20.030
Yeah, but countering it 
probably isn't possible,

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.790
because they're such an
 inexperienced battery.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:27.090
Instead of making them worry 
by firing information at them,

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.700
we have to hope that Hikaru's monster 
pitches will make any squeeze attempt fail.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.210
It's a squeeze!

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:34.330
<i>What?</i>

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.750
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:40.920
A wild pitch!

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:44.720
Don't close your eyes.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.190
Keep your eye on the ball.

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:50.350
Don't be scared of it!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.580
A catcher uses his body to stop the ball!

00:20:57.590 --> 00:20:58.110
He stopped it!

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.940
Move!

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.290
Out!

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:15.530
All right!

00:21:15.530 --> 00:21:17.040
Yes!

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:19.390
Daigo!

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:21.640
Good one, Shigeno!

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.970
Is your hand okay, Daigo-kun?

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:26.770
It's totally fine.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:28.620
We just need one more out.

00:21:30.270 --> 00:21:31.470
<i>I wasn't expecting that.</i>

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:35.760
<i>That play was courageous, especially 
as it's his first time wearing the mask.</i>

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:38.230
Two outs!

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.860
Let's finish this!

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:44.660
<i>He might have the most 
important thing a catcher needs.</i>

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.200
Strike!

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:54.020
Strike! Out!

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:55.960
That's game!

00:22:03.310 --> 00:22:04.300
<i>We won.</i>

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:06.940
Hikaru!

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:10.140
<i>We were able to win because of Daigo-kun!</i>

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:21.650
<i>And now, I finally feel like 
I'm part of the Dolphins!</i>

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:25.280
Finally... finally...

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.150
Mifune

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:27.150
Tanikawa

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:28.150
Thank you for the game!

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:01.660
Yes!

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:03.540
We made it past the first round!

00:24:03.870 --> 00:24:06.250
Hikaru and I made our battery debut, too!

00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:09.580
We can't rest on our laurels, though.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:13.030
We've got so much work to do before
next week's second-round matchup.

00:24:13.590 --> 00:24:16.730
Which reminds me... Sakura's spent 
the whole time sitting on the bench.

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:18.650
Is that really okay?

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Mutsuko's Melancholy

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:21.920
Next time: "Mutsuko's Melancholy."

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.530
Run to the stage of your dreams!
